// Test Description: Statement following a nested if/else whose both branches contain another if/else
// Category: control
// Dependencies: none
// Expected: PASS
//
// Regression for COMPILER-CODEGEN-DROPS-STATEMENT-AFTER-NESTED-IF (the root
// cause of COMPILER-PLUGIN-ASSEMBLE-HANGS-ON-PAGE-PROJECTS): when an
// `if/else` was nested inside another `if/else` and both inner branches
// contained yet another `if/else`, the codegen's `collect_jump_targets`
// stopped at the innermost merge block instead of chasing the Jump chain
// to the eventual continuation, so the OUTER statement after the nested
// if/else got short-circuited on `generated.contains(...)` and was dropped
// from the emitted WASM entirely. frame.ui's `process_text_node` had this
// exact shape; the `remaining = remaining.substring(...)` reassignment
// that advances its `while` loop was the dropped statement, so the loop
// ran forever (bounded only by the safety counter the plugin author added
// as a workaround).
//
// Expected output (one line per printl):
//   inner-a
//   AFTER

start:
	if true
		if true
			if true
				printl("inner-a")
			else
				printl("inner-b")
		else
			if true
				printl("inner-c")
			else
				printl("inner-d")

		printl("AFTER")
